{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_b34717bdbb32495789555bb9","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"grep -n -i -A4 \"dedup\\|bd create\\|bd search\\|file\\b\\|--file\\|existing\\|bd_failure\" openspec/changes/add-fault-ticket-routing/design.md | head -80","timeout":15},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"13:  deduplicated, with provenance back to the scenario and report row.\n14-- Non-Goals: agent faults are never routed (they inform AIX work in genesis,\n15-  per the taxonomy — that is a human decision); no cross-repo DB writes\n16:  beyond `bd create` in the target repo; no GitHub issue filing (beads is the\n17-  source of truth in every family repo).\n18-\n19-## Decisions\n20-\n21:### 1. Filing via `bd create` in the target repo working directory\n22-\n23:beads runs embedded with `no-db: true` per repo; the only correct way to file\n24:into `../wai` is to run `bd create` with that repo as cwd. Token budget is\n25-irrelevant (no model call); exit-code checking + parsed issue id is captured\n26-for the `routed` summary. Process-boundary scoring principle applies to\n27-ourselves: we assert on exit codes and output, never on `bd` internals.\n28-\n29:### 2. Deduplication by fingerprint token, searched in the target repo\n30-\n31-A fault is (scenario, fault-class, tool). The token\n32-`evallerina:<scenario>:<fault-class>` goes in the ticket body (the tool\n33-version goes in the body too, not the token — a recurring fault on a new\n--\n35:`bd search --status open <token>` in the target repo (`bd list` + grep with\n36-the same status filter as fallback). Closed issues are deliberately no\n37:match: `bd search` includes closed issues by default, so the status filter\n38-must be pinned, and a fault that regresses after its ticket was closed is\n39:re-filed rather than suppressed. Any open match → decision `existing`. This mirrors how\n40-evallerina-54f already propagated (\"same drift class as evallerina-54f\" in\n41-espectacular's tracker) — the token makes that linkage machine-readable.\n42-\n43-### 5. `bd` failure in a mapped repo is `skipped`, never fatal\n--\n45:Filing is an optimization over the report, not a gate: if `bd create` fails\n46-in the target repository (not a beads repo, `bd` binary missing, repo\n47:locked), the decision is `skipped` with reason `bd_failure`, the reason is\n48-recorded in the proposal row, and the report completes. The dashboard\n49-already surfaces the fault; a broken tracker must not crash the rotation or\n50-mask a `filed` count that did not happen.\n51-\n--\n59: \"decision\": \"dry_run|filed|existing|skipped\", \"reason\": null,\n60- \"bd_issue_id\": null, \"row_provenance\": {\"scenario\": \"...\", \"model\": \"...\", \"tool\": \"...\"}}\n61-```\n62-\n63:`reason` is null except for `skipped` (`unmapped_tool`, `bd_failure`);\n64-`bd_issue_id` is set only for `filed`. The CI artifact is reviewable without\n65-reading code.\n66-\n67:### 3. Dry-run default, `--file` behind an explicit flag\n68-\n69:Scheduled/CI runs must never file tickets (conservative authority policy).\n70-`--route` alone produces `proposed-tickets.jsonl` (decision `dry_run` for\n71:every row above threshold); `--route --file` additionally shells out to `bd`.\n72-This keeps the nightly artifact reviewable before any cross-repo write.\n73-\n74-### 4. Tool → repo mapping is a committed `routing.toml`\n75-\n--\n96:- `bd create` in a foreign repo mutates another project's tracker → mitigated\n97:  by dry-run default + fingerprint dedup + `--file` opt-in.\n98-- Tool attribution in live rows is currently hardcoded; routing keys on the\n99-  scenario's recorded tool (Decision 4) and carries the row tool only as\n100-  provenance, so attribution drift routes to the wrong ticket *text*, never\n101-  the wrong repo.\n102:- Rate: a bad nightly run could propose many tickets → the existing routing\n103-  threshold (min(3, registry)) is reused so only faults reproducible across\n104-  the configured minimum get proposed.\n105-- Sibling checkouts may not exist in CI → `skipped`, artifact still uploaded.\n106-\n--\n110:2. Wire `--file` + tests in a second commit (red→green per task ordering).\n111-3. Update GHA tier-2 workflow to upload `proposed-tickets.jsonl`.\n112-\n113-## Open Questions\n114-\n115:- None. `--file` authority is granted by the human invoking it locally.\n"}],"details":{}}}
