if `bd create` fails\n46-in the target repository (not a beads repo, `bd` binary missing, repo\n47:locked), the decision is `skipped` with reason `bd_failure`, the reason is\n48-recorded in the proposal row, and the report completes. The dashboard\n49-already surfaces the fault; a broken tracker must not crash the rotation or\n50-mask a `filed` count that did not happen.\n51-\n--\n59: \"decision\": \"dry_run|filed|existing|skipped\", \"reason\": null,\n60- \"bd_issue_id\": null, \"row_provenance\": {\"scenario\": \"...\", \"model\": \"...\", \"tool\": \"...\"}}\n61-```\n62-\n63:`reason` is null except for `skipped` (`unmapped_tool`, `bd_failure`);\n64-`bd_issue_id` is set only for `filed`. The CI artifact is reviewable without\n65-reading code.\n66-\n67:### 3. Dry-run default, `--file` behind an explicit flag\n68-\n69:Scheduled/CI runs must never file tickets (conservative authority policy).\n70-`--route` alone produces `proposed-tickets.jsonl` (decision `dry_run` for\n71:every row above threshold); `--route --file` additionally shells out to `bd`.\n72-This keeps the nightly artifact reviewable before any cross-repo write.\n73-\n74-### 4. Tool → repo mapping is a committed `routing.toml`\n75-\n--\n96:- `bd create` in a foreign repo mutates another project's tracker → mitigated\n97:  by dry-run default + fingerprint dedup + `--file` opt-in.\n98-- Tool attribution in live rows is currently hardcoded; routing keys on the\n99-  scenario's recorded tool (Decision 4) and carries the row tool only as\n100-  provenance, so attribution drift routes to the wrong ticket *text*, never\n101-  the wrong repo.\n102:- Rate: a bad nightly run could propose many tickets → the existing routing\n103-  threshold (min(3, registry)) is reused so only faults reproducible across\n104-  the configured minimum get proposed.\n105-- Sibling checkouts may not exist in CI → `skipped`, artifact still uploaded.\n106-\n--\n110:2. Wire `--file` + tests in a second commit (red→green per task ordering).\n111-3. Update GHA tier-2 workflow to upload `proposed-tickets.jsonl`.\n112-\n113-## Open Questions\n114-\n115:- None. `--file` authority is granted by the human invoking it locally.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792427453227}}
