in place; loud errors only for... design says bd failure never fatal. Errors like missing bd binary → spawn err → treated as bd_failure? Design: \\\"`bd` binary missing\\\" → skipped/bd_failure. So spawn errors also map to bd_failure for create. For search, if bd search fails (non-beads dir)? Not spec'd... If repo isn't a beads repo, search fails → treat like no match → then create fails → skipped/bd_failure. That composes fine.\\n\\nNow bd CLI behavior — let me experiment in temp dir:\\n- `bd init` (what flags? maybe `bd init --no-db`? The charly repo config has no-db: true. Let's see what `bd init` produces and what search output looks like.)\\n- `bd create \\\"title\\\" --body`? check flags.\\n- `bd search --status open <query>` — does it match body?\\n- `bd list --status open` output format.\\n\\nAlso HOME isolation: bd might use a global ~/.beads or config. Let's test.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Design understood. Now let me experiment with `bd` CLI behavior in an isolated temp dir to learn its exact outputs (init, create, search, export)."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c46923d254cb4153849d07bd","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"export T=$(mktemp -d); cd $T\ngit init -q repo && cd repo\nbd init 2>&1 | head -5\necho \"--- config:\"; cat .beads/config.yaml 2>/dev/null\necho \"--- create:\"; bd create \"Test token evallerina:scen:tool_fault in body\" --body \"token here evallerina:scen:tool_fault\" 2>&1 | head -5\necho \"--- search open:\"; bd search --status open \"evallerina:scen:tool_fault\" 2>&1 | head -10\necho \"--- close + search:\"; bd list 2>&1 | head -5","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1061,"output":1025,"cacheRead":19712,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":835,"totalTokens":21798,"cost":{"input":0.00015915,"output":0.0005124999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00059136,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00126301}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":179242745322